{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists","id":983721,"title":"Mixing up Antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-07T20:26:53-07:00","id":983721,"title":"Mixing up Antagonists","content":"Aside from &quot;evil&quot; versions of themselves, each of the Supernaturals has a specific opponent they face: Vampires have the Strix, Werewolves have the Hosts/Ridden/Idigam, Mages have Abyssal Entities, Sin-Eaters have...who/whatever they have to deal with. But suppose they occasionally run into each others' enemies? Who would you be most interested in seeing go up against each?<br /> Are there any you think each would be particularly effective or ineffective against? <br /> <br /> Kindred vs. Heroes? Mages vs. Idigams? Changelings vs. Pandorans? Beasts vs. Gentry? Go nuts!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T21:15:07-07:00","id":983747,"title":"","content":"Demon Storyteller's Guide has a section that sorta talks about this with things like Strix corrupting infrastructure and angels trying to invade the hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:26:07-07:00","id":983780,"title":"","content":"It's hard to imagine anyone really dealing with an idigam.<br /> <br /> I've put some Pandorans in other games but you have to fidget the rules around since they go dormant unless there's a Promethean nearby, after some time.<br /> <br /> Claimed work pretty easily across the board. Ridden and urged too.<br /> <br /> The hosts mesh well with a few. Hunter, vampire, and mage at least. They're capable of being a city-destroying threat, but still be encountered individually and in swarms without them ripping peoples souls from their bodies like Pez from a dispenser. As an added benefit they are very insidious foe, and can take over touchstones and other mortal contacts. Nothing keeps them from hollowing out supernaturals, either. They certainly could be a threat in Promethean, Changeling and Demon but I think it would sort of diminish the themes of the games. I could see Beasts working along with them against werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:05:06-07:00","id":983799,"title":"","content":"How about Huntsmen vs Mages? Not just in the sense of a direct fight, but also in a race to track down a given Changeling?<br /> <br /> Another that comes to mind is a Begotten character against an Idigam. The former would be trying to rally her Kin in the region against the latter as it becomes more dangerous with time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T05:49:27-07:00","id":983869,"title":"","content":"I think Hosts, especially the big two, work well for vampires. Azlu have the spider's coils, conspiracy, and stifling angle going on; while Beshilu have the decay and disease thing going.<br /> <br /> By contrast, I think Idigam would work better for mages - reality's a lie after all, which adds a new perspective to how cavalier the idigam are about its rules - might some mages be seduced?<br /> <br /> Strix could work pretty well for Sineaters. They transgress life and death, walk around in dead bodies, and aren't as easy to deal with as ghosts. They're also an enemy of <i>this</i> world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T05:57:05-07:00","id":983875,"title":"","content":"Acamoth vs Beasts<br /> Idigam vs Mummies<br /> Abmortals vs Werewolves (Abmortals usually are personally scary, but are extremely hard to kill with mere violence)<br /> Sublimati vs Vampires","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:29:34-07:00","id":983947,"title":"","content":"Gulmoths vs. Werewolves (To a Werewolf they're something even more wrong then the Igidam).<br /> Hunters vs. Huntsmen (This has happened in Tokyo).<br /> Mages vs. The Hosts (Hosts are messing majorly with the Gauntlet, pissing off Mages who use the Spirit Arcana).<br /> Promeathans vs. Strix (Strix tries to ride their bodies, doesn't work put as planned)<br /> Mummy vs. True Fae (Immortal Enemies down through millenia)<br /> Changeling vs. Alchemists (Alchemists want to steal and use goblin fruits in they're alchemy).<br /> Sin Eater vs. Bound Supernal Shades (because it'd be interesting). Or Liches (because a Lich who tries to take a Sin Eaters soul will find someone has already claimed it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-08-2016, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T13:35:28-07:00","id":984038,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters vs. Striges: It's a seemingly ghost-like being, with powers over death, but the normal anti-ghost measures won't work. The longer you take to subdue it, the more time it has to make pissed-off ghosts and possess things.<br /> <br /> Prometheans vs. Angels: Prometheans create chaos in their wake, and their Wasteland would undoubtedly screw with infrastructure. The similarity between Angel and Qashmal serves to dredge up some cosmological confusion for the Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T13:50:32-07:00","id":984045,"title":"","content":"I've had some fun in my home game pitting my mages against an Amkhata. The bad news is that it eats Artifacts, the good news is it's not difficult for mages to get their hands on enchanted firepower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T00:24:35-07:00","id":984291,"title":"","content":"I just finished a Mage chronicle where I used several Strix as antagonists. The Mages were trying to prevent the escape of one of the Bound, with all of the tragedy that would entail, while the Strix, who are drawn to imminent disaster, where doing there best to make sure the show did go on. What worked best was that the Strix are neither Spirits or Ghosts, meaning they didn't fall neatly into the cookie cutter holes the Mages tried to stuff them in. It was nice not being able to wave their wands and make all of their problems disappear.<br /> \u200bI did throw Pandorans at some Mages in my first chronicle but that was just because the Mages came between them and their Promethean prey. All the Mages really needed to do was step out of the way but they didn't know that.<br /> \u200bMixing the antagonists like this can be difficult, but the fact that they weren't tailor made for the abilities of the splat makes them more challenging, more of an unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:02:19-07:00","id":984401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=984291#post984291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just finished a Mage chronicle where I used several Strix as antagonists. The Mages were trying to prevent the escape of one of the Bound, with all of the tragedy that would entail, while the Strix, who are drawn to imminent disaster, where doing there best to make sure the show did go on. What worked best was that the Strix are neither Spirits or Ghosts, meaning they didn't fall neatly into the cookie cutter holes the Mages tried to stuff them in. It was nice not being able to wave their wands and make all of their problems disappear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that disadvantage would be tempered by fairly easy access to fire and sunlight on the Mages' part, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:45:31-07:00","id":984436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=984401#post984401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose that disadvantage would be tempered by fairly easy access to fire and sunlight on the Mages' part, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Once the Mages know that's effective against the Strix, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T18:29:22-07:00","id":987527,"title":"","content":"Who are Sublimati, Huntsmen and Striges? For that matter, what are &quot;the Unfleshed&quot;??<br /> <br /> The Death Arcana should affect the Strix just fine, as it works on creatures with a shadow-nature.<br /> <br /> The Gentry abduct mortals, ripping their souls away in the process. Is there any canonical support for them attempting to take other Supernaturals? What if they have weak souls, like the Created or vampires? Also, I kinda got the impression that Mummy's Judges are really Antagonists, from a certain pov, is that true? About how powerful are they?<br /> <br /> On another tangent: The World of Darkness is large, but each player splat has several enemies, who surely bump up against each other more often. What such encounters can you imagine?<br /> <br /> If Shuankhsen, Bale Hounds and Scelesti should happen to meet, are they likely to compete against each other, or join forces? I'm blanking on who would be an interesting meeting for a Centimanti, any ideas? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:06:20-07:00","id":987540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=987527#post987527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Shuankhsen, Bale Hounds and Scelesti should happen to meet, are they likely to compete against each other, or join forces? I'm blanking on who would be an interesting meeting for a Centimanti, any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>A particularly monstrous Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:08:42-07:00","id":987542,"title":"","content":"Sublimati are Pandorans that have achieved intelligence and sapience by consuming Vitriol. Huntsmen are from Changeling second edition, they bring back Changelings. Stirges are strix, shadow-owls that delight in tormenting and teaching vampires. Unfleshed are Prometheans made of entirely artificial structures, such as a robot.<br /> <br /> I don't believe the Gentry did attempt to take other supernaturals in first edition. They were aware of them but presumably they wouldn't be as malleable as a raw human.<br /> <br /> In werewolf, the beshilu and azlu aren't fans of one another.<br /> <br /> Bale Hounds and Scelesti wouldn't like each other. The Abyss and Inferno are apparently at odds. The Abyss wants to destroy what is for what they are, the Inferno just wants to corrupt it. You can't corrupt if it isn't there.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Centimani would work well with the Pure, providing the situation was right. Also the Circle of the Crone and, of course, Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:00:07-07:00","id":987567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=987542#post987542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine the Centimani would work well with the Pure, providing the situation was right.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least until Disquiet inevitably sets in and sets one of the Wolves into a Rage.<br /> <br /> That said, I could see a triple team-up of Inferno-binding Mages, Balehounds and Belial's Brood, with a little Begotten sprinkled in for good measure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:14:55-07:00","id":987846,"title":"","content":"I personally like imagining what happens when hunter groups from the supplement and fan books, specifically designed to go after a specific splat, get set against another monster.<br /> <br /> Just an easy example, the Barrett Commission. Say you're a changeling, and you know about hunters. So you take all the precautions you can to make sure you stay low and never attract violent attention. Then one day you find a lien on what property you might have, your money is literally worthless paper in your wallet, and someone has you on a warrant from before your Durance. That's terrifying, because they somehow found you, not your fetch, and connected it to you. So now your Mask is worthless, because they didn't bother to try seeing through it. It's a nice twist when a splat in it's comfort zone violently gets ripped into a new situation against something using their own tricks, or all new tricks, against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T16:54:21-07:00","id":988009,"title":"","content":"I used a Seer of the Paternoster in a Vampire Chronicle once.<br /> <br /> It ended with most of the Coterie dead, and the Sanctified Daeva kissing the hand of the Seer.<br /> <br /> Everyone loved it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T22:45:13-07:00","id":988139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=987542#post987542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sublimati are Pandorans that have achieved intelligence and sapience by consuming Vitriol. Huntsmen are from Changeling second edition, they bring back Changelings. Stirges are strix, shadow-owls that delight in tormenting and teaching vampires. Unfleshed are Prometheans made of entirely artificial structures, such as a robot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know the Strix, I just thought &quot;Strix&quot; was alsothe plural! Huntsmen are a form of Fae, or something else? Unfleshed are mechanical Prometheans? Like, they could be confused for an angel/demon?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't believe the Gentry did attempt to take other supernaturals in first edition. They were aware of them but presumably they wouldn't be as malleable as a raw human. </div> </div> </div>If WW wants to resist mixing the splats, I guess they'd just say that there's something in supernatural souls that resists making the Oaths necessary to bind one's essence to Arcadia for survival...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Bale Hounds and Scelesti wouldn't like each other. The Abyss and Inferno are apparently at odds. The Abyss wants to destroy what is for what they are, the Inferno just wants to corrupt it. You can't corrupt if it isn't there. </div> </div> </div>I thought Bale Hounds served the Maeljin Incarnae...are they linked to the Inferno and its demons?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T22:48:59-07:00","id":988140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=987846#post987846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally like imagining what happens when hunter groups from the supplement and fan books, specifically designed to go after a specific splat, get set against another monster.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>This has me imagining an encounter between a Lucifuge hunter and an Unchained:<br /> <br /> Demon: &quot;Oh! You thought I was...no, sorry, I'm really a &quot;demon&quot; demon...We just, sort of, call ourselves that...and use lots of demonic terms without really being demonic, you know?&quot;<br /> <br /> Lucifuge: &quot;Sooo...basically, you're totally misappropriating my culture?&quot;<br /> <br /> Demon: &quot;...Maaaybe?&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T22:55:20-07:00","id":988141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=988139#post988139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen are a form of Fae, or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're sort of spirit-y incorporeal entities of hunting from Arcadia that fae grab, force into physical form (which they hate) and send them out to collect changelings. They are sort of immortal, near perfect shapechangers and make for rather.... different antagonists compared to most foes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfleshed are mechanical Prometheans? Like, they could be confused for an angel/demon? </div> </div> </div>I guess, though angels and demons can look like a lot of things. I mean, an angel or demon will probably have much more organic parts than an unfleshed has (and many angels/demons don't have any mechanical parts). Another thing they could be mistaken as would be deviants, metalflesh changelings (and elemental changelings that happen to have metal as their element), robot geotia, mechanical spirits, skinwalkers that can shapechange into mechanical spirits, sin-eaters with the industrial key, etc. There is a decent amount of things that can look like robots.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:07:33-07:00","id":988147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=988140#post988140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has me imagining an encounter between a Lucifuge hunter and an Unchained:<br /> <br /> Demon: &quot;Oh! You thought I was...no, sorry, I'm really a &quot;demon&quot; demon...We just, sort of, call ourselves that...and use lots of demonic terms without really being demonic, you know?&quot;<br /> <br /> Lucifuge: &quot;Sooo...basically, you're totally misappropriating my culture?&quot;<br /> <br /> Demon: &quot;...Maaaybe?&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>According to the lucifuge's definition of a demon; Geotia of Saints, Cheribum, Pope Ghosts, and Faith Spirits are all demons. So I'm pretty sure it's the lucifuge who are using the wrong terms. :P<br /> <br /> Though interestingly, according to the books Lucifuge do know a tonne about GM-Demons and GM-Angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-16-2016, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T23:30:12-07:00","id":988153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=988141#post988141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're sort of spirit-y incorporeal entities of hunting from Arcadia that fae grab, force into physical form (which they hate) and send them out to collect changelings. They are sort of immortal, near perfect shapechangers and make for rather.... different antagonists compared to most foes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving some context to this:<br /> <br /> In 1e, the True Fae vied against one another for Titles, massive Contracts with the Wyrd that allow them to manifest in Arcadia without risking their very being, through narrative conflicts called Legends, with the stakes generally being the Titles they used to engage in a given contest.<br /> <br /> Typically, a Fae can only be challenged to Legend combat by the Fae who holds the claim to that Title, initially by being the one to describe that Fae in a fitting manner. The most dangerous exception to this restriction is if one of the Fae in a Legend falters in their description; the resulting &quot;Dread Gap&quot; allows <i>any</i> Fae to seize control of the narrative and either claim the prize for victory or fail without incurring personal loss.<br /> <br /> In 2e, a freehold is founded upon a Bulwark, a ritual based on a story familiar to that part of the world which empowers the Courts with Approaches that effectively restrict the region from access by any Fae who cannot abide by their rules. If this sounds familiar, it's because it's really easy to describe a freehold as an artificial scarecrow-Fae. The Bulwark significantly narrows the range of viable invaders as long as it holds up.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen, then, are the Fae's tools for trying to force a Dread Gap by breaking the Bulwark while they're on their primary duty of retrieving a wayward changeling who's grown in power and status. Their main targets are almost invariably changelings who've built up a couple Approaches, which means they're more expensive to try to bring in in the long run, so they sow discord among the Courts by targeting the least of their nobility and leaning on that best of intimidations, &quot;It's them and theirs or you and yours.&quot;<br /> <br /> The suite of powers and tools they have at their disposal make the fact that they work on a time limit very fortunate for the Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:44:52-07:00","id":988171,"title":"","content":"I haven't kept up with a lot of NWoD supplements, but I do know that they teased Werewolf fans early on with a book seemingly about Fera, but that was really about various unique ways that mortals could transform into bestial forms. Did WW ever decide that they'd jerked us around enough and give us REAL Changing Breeds, actual Bastet/Werecats, Weresnakes, Werelizards, etc?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T02:10:17-07:00","id":988190,"title":"","content":"It's called <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/51348/World-of-Darkness-Changing-Breeds\" target=\"_blank\">Changing Breeds</a>. But it's cursed. If mentioned, someone will inevitably post about how they think it's bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T04:19:40-07:00","id":988204,"title":"","content":"There's also more toolbox-type rules for Fera in War Against The Pure. <br /> <br /> Also a few of us are kind of hoping for Changing Breeds 2E: We Didn't Fuck It Up This Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T05:47:27-07:00","id":988213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=988139#post988139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Bale Hounds served the Maeljin Incarnae...are they linked to the Inferno and its demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Inferno says yes (and also that the Lucifuge are children of Inferno demons - also the Spirit Slayers Hunter supplement says werewolves tend to regard Lucifuge as children of the Maeljin). So the connection is as explicit as the NWoD/ChroD ever got/gets.<br /> <br /> Doesn't mean you have to abide by it of course, but I personally like the connection, not least because I like keeping the number of &quot;first causes&quot; as low as possible. It does mean that Bale Hounds and their entourage work for everything the Inferno does. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Do slashers count as hunters' antagonists? A villain representing the worst humanity has to offer - with the possibility but not certainty that they're ot quite human any more - is a good thing to pit against monsters who are specfically contrasted with humans. Vampires, Prometheans, maybe Unchained. For demons, it seems like the Brutes or Geniuses would be the best - the extremes of mindlessness or plans within plans. For Prometheans, Freaks or Charmers - wrong like Prometheans are, or a cavalier abuse of the connectivity Prometheans long for. For vampires, Avengers are low-hanging fruit (even more so if they've targeted the vampire for something that's not specifically vampiric), or Geniuses (plans within plans again).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T06:55:04-07:00","id":988231,"title":"","content":"The God Machine versus the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T10:08:17-07:00","id":988296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=988231#post988231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God Machine versus the Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really abstract, confusing matchup, which I kind of like. I mean, it's basically the <i>personified concept of oppression</i> being placed in opposition to the <i>personified act of oppressing</i>. After a while, it'd probably be pretty impossible to tell who was winning and which side was what.<br /> <br /> Anyone swept up in such a confrontation could easily be fighting for both sides without even realizing there were sides to fight on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:30:29-07:00","id":988872,"title":"","content":"Hell the two <i>sides</i> might not realise it for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:10:11-07:00","id":992138,"title":"","content":"Don't know very much about the &quot;crossing of streams&quot; with nemesis, but came across stuff that could make for some pretty awesome bridge between the strix, kindred themselves and something else altogether <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lightning_bird\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> What i have done is adapt a number of critters from Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss and Skinchangers to my Requiem game as either antagonists or dangerous obstacles/opportunities to be dealt with depending on circunstances and the PCs own cunning and imagination. Have also reskinned a bunch of stuff from old books like Antagonists, Second Sight &amp; Mythologies, sometimes mixing with concepts from other books, to create somewhat more complicated, nuanced or powerful adversaries to deal with...<br /> <br /> - Like a family of supermodel-socialites and businessmen inspired in the Kardashians with influence on Abbey Road that actually composes a powerful clan/cult of Aswangs and part of the Cheiron Group's board of directors,<br /> <br /> - Citadels of undead, some possibly from the time of the Camarilla or even before existing in weird places outside the mundane that might be either Book of Dead's underworld, the Woundgate from Mirrors or something between and while sustaining themselves in the other side, require some things they can only acquire in the world of sunlight and the living.<br /> <br /> - Eerie black cats, glittering spirit snakes, somber hellhounds or silver-tongued beings dressed in the guise of one's own broken reflection or Death itself, who will offer a mockery of life and power as blood-drinking undead to those ambitious, desperate or perverted enough to pay the peculiar prices of their favors.<br /> <br /> - A secret experiment of human cloning that goes immensely wrong, spawning an army of pandoran-esque radiactive mockeries that massacres its makers to then &quot;liberate&quot; their corpses and initiate a crusade to cleanse the Earth from humanity through its &quot;reanimator army&quot; and its strange collectivity.<br /> <br /> And so on. I love to come with slowly building up weirdness that eventually explodes into some over-the-top Evil Dead-esque climax or worse.<br /> But that's how i roll, back and forth on the pulpiness all the way. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-17-2016, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:14:42-07:00","id":993660,"title":"","content":"[sarcasm] I am sure a sin-eater wouldn't be deeply offended/outraged to the point of violence if a Strix was using a dead friend as a meat suit, and Strix being incredibly reasonable and humane wouldn't react badly to that at all.[/sarcasm]<br /> <br /> Most of the activities of the various antagonist creatures wouldn't solely draw the attention of only one supernatural subculture. At very least there will be individuals interested in any major disruption to the status quo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-26-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T22:21:14-07:00","id":998620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=993660#post993660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[sarcasm] I am sure a sin-eater wouldn't be deeply offended/outraged to the point of violence if a Strix was using a dead friend as a meat suit, and Strix being incredibly reasonable and humane wouldn't react badly to that at all.[/sarcasm]<br /> <br /> Most of the activities of the various antagonist creatures wouldn't solely draw the attention of only one supernatural subculture. At very least there will be individuals interested in any major disruption to the status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>All too true. And the conscientious/idealistic/moralistic might even end up getting themselves more of that kind of trouble than they would prefer otherwise, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T23:48:27-07:00","id":998633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=988296#post988296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's really abstract, confusing matchup, which I kind of like. I mean, it's basically the <i>personified concept of oppression</i> being placed in opposition to the <i>personified act of oppressing</i>. After a while, it'd probably be pretty impossible to tell who was winning and which side was what.<br /> <br /> Anyone swept up in such a confrontation could easily be fighting for both sides without even realizing there were sides to fight on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think that that sort of conflict really depends on what you decide the relationship between the Exarchs and the God-Machine is. Is the GM the apparatus of the Lie gone rogue? An extra-dimensional/temporal infection reordering the universe on its alien principles? An especially canny Old God playing the long game to try and retake it's throne? Because a war like that depends a lot of how much of the other sides capabilities each faction knows.<br /> <br /> On the street level, the fight would be utterly byzantine and so subtle most agents don't even know there's a game, let alone what it is (the Exarch's can retroactively change history from on high, and the G-M has more or less tactical time reversal tech and angels who live outside of normal space-time. So the name of the game is winning a point before the other side even notices you're making a play). OR it would just be downright apocalyptic, complete with meteor strikes, super-viruses and world war 3 as everyone races to wipe out the other sides key infrastructure and C&amp;C nodes before they lose the capability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11821-st-just","name":"St.Just","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T22:19:30-07:00","id":999069,"title":"","content":"Just to expand further, what do you guys think of when you add fan-game antagonits into the mix against other official and fan splats? Because for my own part, I can see a lot of splats having a lot of trouble if they go up against Lemurian geniuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T02:23:41-08:00","id":999133,"title":"","content":"I know it was mentioned earlier, but now I really want to see a chronicle where an Elder Kindred is in a shadow war with an Elder Sublimati. One trying to scare off or eliminate the other's source of Pyros, the other quelling their rival's herd and influence. All the while the PCs are cought in the middle. It would be just fantastic! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T04:48:57-08:00","id":999162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=999069#post999069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to expand further, what do you guys think of when you add fan-game antagonits into the mix against other official and fan splats? Because for my own part, I can see a lot of splats having a lot of trouble if they go up against Lemurian geniuses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or Leviathan cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:46:52-08:00","id":999308,"title":"","content":"The game I'm STing for now includes Beasts facing off with Hosts, Mages secretly using Azlu to keep a Wound closed off, and Changelings dealing with The God Machine trying to close off Arcadia, while Demons keep blasting new hedge gates.<br /> <br /> In the werewolf game I'm playing in, we've got a low synergy sin-eater after our pack leader, we pissed off a Mad mage. And we might or might not be awakening Cthulu. Jury's still out on what the effects of our last session were, but we're mostly certain the void entity is cthulu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T08:33:14-08:00","id":1018462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=999162#post999162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=999069#post999069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to expand further, what do you guys think of when you add fan-game antagonits into the mix against other official and fan splats? Because for my own part, I can see a lot of splats having a lot of trouble if they go up against Lemurian geniuses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or Leviathan cults.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good points - damn, there's a bunch of official stuff i haven't even scratched the surface of in my games yet, so i guess years might go by before i even seriously read on some of those... Still toying with the Nonnati, cthonic pre-human Ur-vampires cobbled together from bits of Mythologies, Predators, Intruders and some other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-17-2016, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T14:27:13-08:00","id":1018587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=999162#post999162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or Leviathan cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leviathan Cults could be a really good adversary for Nobility, since they're basically a perversion of the very concepts of community and cooperation that Nobility hold dear, in several fundamental ways. Especially if the cult itself is uncomfortably close in belief or ideology to what the Princesses in question but more extreme and violent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T06:15:45-08:00","id":1018786,"title":"","content":"As an aside, has anyone ever tried <b>mashing up</b> antagonists, like making the Strix the agents of some forgotten True Fae (Changeling) or Kerberoi (Geist), if not fragments of such a being, or some other unholy blend of different brands of Nemeses, such as Idigam coming from the Abyss, Astral Realm or the Lower Depths?<br /> <br /> Just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T23:31:17-08:00","id":1019108,"title":"","content":"Going a little further out of main field here, but the Necromancy Discipline, offered in <i>The Vampire Translation Guide</i> for the Requiem version of clan Giovanni, would make them great antagonists for Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> These are vampires who can sense and interact with ghosts in Twilight, enter Twilight directly, read final visions off corpses, command ghosts, summon them from Twilight and the Underworld, send living mortal souls into Twilight and let ghosts possess the empty body, and even open Avernian Gates. Sin-Eaters would side-eye these guys so hard, because what the hell, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T10:15:25-08:00","id":1023334,"title":"","content":"Mages hunting after the Dark Mother, Beasts trying to raid a Watchtower and Dracula interfering with the Autumn Court's latest activities, that sort of thing sounds pretty interesting, too, mainly because those things are legendary and not exactly &quot;Antagonists&quot;.<br /> <br /> In general, putting the characters in hostile, unusual places or a hostile force in their own 'domain' seems fun: A Sin-Eater might not feel weird about going into the underworld, most Changelings however probably would. Set Shuankhsen lose in the Hedge, have Privateers stumble around in the Shadow, Centimani raiding a Mummy's Cult, and Strix furthering Infrastructure. &quot;What the hell are they? What are they doing HERE? How did they get here? WHY are they doing that?&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:53:05-08:00","id":1023873,"title":"","content":"I don't think mashing up antagonists is ever a bad idea, so long as you don't have them in-character bs each other. Like if you somehow have Belial's Brood and the Seers working together, they're both going to know it's at best an alliance of convenience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T12:29:30-08:00","id":1023890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/983721-mixing-up-antagonists?p=1023873#post1023873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think mashing up antagonists is ever a bad idea, so long as you don't have them in-character bs each other. Like if you somehow have Belial's Brood and the Seers working together, they're both going to know it's at best an alliance of convenience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also known as Betrayal-Chicken: who screws over who first.<br /> <br /> &quot;Curse your sudden but inevitable betrayal!&quot; -Wash","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}